{
  "_provenance": "Additive batch (2026-08-22): missing laureates from two closed award lists -- AIA Gold Medal (1907-2026) and Pritzker Architecture Prize (1979-2026), diffed against the live graph/data person nodes (763 persons at time of research). Includes all 36 missing Pritzker laureates and a Tier-1 subset of 10 missing Gold Medal laureates (canonical 20th-century modern-movement figures with strong ties to the existing lineage era: Mazria, Calatrava, Legorreta, Erickson, Caudill, Harrison, Nervi, Aalto, Le Corbusier, Ralph Walker); Tange, Piano, and Murcutt already covered via the Pritzker set also get a second honor edge to h-aia-gold-medal since they won both. Deferred to a future pre-1950 Beaux-Arts/honorary-era Gold Medal batch (lower connectivity to the current dataset, harder to verify quickly, mostly honorary foreign recipients): Dudok, Delano, Perret, Abercrombie, Maginnis, Ostberg, Medary, Shaw, Lutyens, Goodhue, Bacon, Laloux, Swartwout, Webb. Excluded outright: Thomas Jefferson (1993 co-honoree) -- posthumous/honorary, not a practicing figure in this lineage graph. No new practice nodes added: Herzog & de Meuron, SANAA, and Alvaro Siza's practice already existed as orphaned MCHAP-batch practice nodes with no person links, so principal edges were added to connect the new person nodes to them instead of creating duplicates; RCR Arquitectes, Grafton Architects, and Lacaton & Vassal are represented via person-to-person partner edges only, matching the dominant existing convention (e.g. skidmore/owings/merrill) rather than the newer practice-node pattern. Rafael Aranda (RCR) required disambiguated id aranda_r to avoid collision with the existing unrelated node 'aranda' (Benjamin Aranda, Aranda\\\\Lasch). Sources: Wikipedia \"AIA Gold Medal\" and \"Pritzker Architecture Prize\" list pages, cross-checked against Wikipedia/Pritzker Prize org bios for recent laureates' birth years.",
